origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:20:    {"id":"AC2","criterion":"A panic triggered inside create_session's wrapped closure (via CREATE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL) is caught by contain_panic and returned to the caller as napi::Result::Err, not an unwind crossing the FFI boundary -- verifiable by calling create_session with the sentinel src_dir and asserting Err is returned rather than the test process aborting.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:21:    {"id":"AC3","criterion":"A panic triggered inside close_session's wrapped closure -- via a CLOSE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL: u32 reserved session_id value, checked inside the contain_panic closure body under #[cfg(test)], mirroring CREATE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL's pattern -- is caught by contain_panic and close_session returns normally (unit type) without the panic propagating to the caller or crashing the host process -- verifiable by calling close_session(CLOSE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL) and asserting the call completes without the test process aborting.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:24:    {"id":"AC6","criterion":"A panic triggered inside extract_all's wrapped closure (via an EXTRACT_ALL_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL added to JsExtractOptions.src_dirs, mirroring the CREATE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL pattern) is caught by contain_panic and the returned Future resolves to napi::Result::Err rather than the spawn_blocking task aborting -- verifiable by awaiting extract_all with the sentinel option and asserting Err is returned rather than the test process aborting. The sentinel may trigger the panic at either the pipeline::extract(...) step or the subsequent JSON-serialization step named in AC1 -- both are required to be inside the guard, and either triggering point satisfies this criterion.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:25:    {"id":"AC7","criterion":"A panic triggered inside initialize_session's wrapped closure -- via an INITIALIZE_SESSION_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL: u32 reserved session_id value, checked inside the contain_panic closure body under #[cfg(test)] (the closure captures session_id for this purpose) -- is caught by contain_panic and the returned Future resolves to napi::Result::Err rather than the spawn_blocking task aborting -- verifiable by awaiting initialize_session with the sentinel session_id and any valid options, and asserting Err is returned rather than the test process aborting. The sentinel check is placed at the point of the existing core call (session.initialize()), after the lookup-or-auto-vivify sequence has completed for a normally-registered session_id -- distinct from AC10's construction-time trigger, which fires during auto-vivified WatchSession construction instead.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:26:    {"id":"AC8","criterion":"A panic triggered inside extract_file_incremental's wrapped closure (via an EXTRACT_FILE_INCREMENTAL_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL file_path, mirroring the same pattern) is caught by contain_panic and the returned Future resolves to napi::Result::Err rather than the spawn_blocking task aborting -- verifiable the same way as AC6. The sentinel check is placed at the point of the existing core call (session.update_file(...)), after the lookup-or-auto-vivify sequence has completed for a normally-registered session_id -- distinct from AC10's construction-time trigger, which fires during auto-vivified WatchSession construction instead.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-BINDING-001.json:28:    {"id":"AC10","criterion":"A panic triggered during auto-vivified WatchSession construction inside initialize_session's or extract_file_incremental's wrapped closure -- via an AUTO_VIVIFY_PANIC_TEST_SENTINEL: u32 reserved session_id value, checked inside the contain_panic closure body before/during WatchSession::new when session_id is not present in SESSIONS -- is caught by contain_panic and the returned Future resolves to napi::Result::Err rather than the spawn_blocking task aborting -- verifiable by awaiting either function with the sentinel session_id (never previously registered via create_session) and asserting Err is returned rather than the test process aborting.","is_error_case":true},
origin/main:.claude/specs/SPEC-CLI-001a.json:31:    { "id": "AC-017", "criterion": "main() is the only site in the crate that calls std::process::exit for a command's own success/failure signaling on the normal (non-Err) path: cmd_extract, cmd_watch, cmd_check, and cmd_inspect each return their exit code as an i32 (or Result<i32>) value from an ordinary function call, assertable directly in a unit test without spawning a subprocess. The sole exception is watch's detached keyboard-input thread, which calls std::process::exit directly with the tracked value described in AC-007/AC-008, since it has no return path back to main(). Any command handler returning Err (config-load failure, missing component, watchexec CriticalError) terminates the process via main()'s own ?-propagation and Rust's Result Termination at exit code 1, not via a direct std::process::exit call anywhere in command-handler code.", "is_error_case": false },
